  "metadata": {
    "title": "Indicative areas remaining in Māori hands by 1890",
    "description": "Highly schematic. Documented strongholds where Māori retained large contiguous blocks against Native Land Court / Crown / private purchase pressure. Not parcel-level. King Country and Central Plateau are merged into a single peanut-shaped polygon (with bridge vertices in the neck region) so the central-North-Island stronghold reads as one continuous area rather than two overlapping blobs; Catmull-Rom smoothing at render time softens the join.",
